__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The live audit log grows on every tool call, including the git commands
# used to check/commit/push this repo — version-controlling it created a
# chase-your-tail loop where checking status was itself a logged (and thus
# repo-dirtying) action. It stays on disk as a real, local, append-only log;
# it's operational data, not source. See RUNBOOK.md §6.
knowledge-vault/audit/tool-calls.jsonl
